# ─── PuppyQ database (Supabase) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Powers the LIVE data on /dams, /sires, /litters, /our-litters, and
# /our-puppies. Without these, those pages render empty ("coming soon"). MUST be
# set both locally (.env.local) AND in Vercel → Settings → Environment Variables.
# Tick BOTH Production and Preview when adding them — a variable scoped to
# Production only builds fine and then renders every live page empty on PR
# previews, which reads as a broken branch. Check any environment at
# /api/puppyq/health.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL         — the project URL, e.g. https://xxxx.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY        — server-only secret key (bypasses RLS).
#                                    NEVER expose to the browser or commit it.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY    — publishable key. REQUIRED for the contact
#                                    form, which writes leads to pawsq and uses
#                                    THIS key only. lib/leads.ts never consults
#                                    the service-role key, even as a fallback:
#                                    that key bypasses RLS and must never sit
#                                    behind a form anyone can submit. Without
#                                    this set, the form still emails and logs
#                                    loudly, but no lead row is written.
# ADAMS_FARM_ORG_ID                — optional. Pin the organization id instead of
#                                    resolving it by name ("Adams Farm Labradoodles").
#
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-secret-key
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-publishable-anon-key
# ADAMS_FARM_ORG_ID=

# ─── Outbound email (the pawsq platform) ────────────────────────────────────
#
# Since 2026-08-30 this site sends NO email itself (pawsq docs/EMAIL.md).
# The contact-form pipeline (spam screening, the lead write, the
# notification email) and the magic-link send all run on the pawsq
# platform (pawsq-app), which sends from adamsfarmlabradoodles@pawsq.com.
# SMTP_EMAIL / SMTP_PASSWORD are gone from this project — the one mailbox
# credential lives on the pawsq-app deployment only.
#
# PAWSQ_PLATFORM_URL — the platform deployment's origin,
#                      e.g. https://puppyq-app.vercel.app (no trailing slash)
# PAWSQ_PLATFORM_KEY — the shared server-to-server secret; the same value
#                      set as PAWSQ_PLATFORM_KEY on the pawsq-app project.
#
# Without these, the contact form still saves leads directly through the
# anon key above (unscreened, logged loudly) and dev sign-in prints the
# magic link to the terminal — degraded, never silent.
#
PAWSQ_PLATFORM_URL=
PAWSQ_PLATFORM_KEY=

# ─── Magic link auth ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# MAGIC_LINK_SECRET  — random secret used to sign login + session tokens.
#                      Generate one with: openssl rand -base64 32
#                      Rotating this invalidates all outstanding links and cookies.
#
# ADAMS_FARM_ALLOWED_EMAILS — comma-separated list of addresses that may access
#                             /forever-families. Removing an address locks them
#                             out immediately (checked on every request).
#                             Example: jane@example.com,bob@example.com
#
# The sign-in link itself is sent by the pawsq platform (PAWSQ_PLATFORM_URL /
# PAWSQ_PLATFORM_KEY above) — nothing further to configure here. Without
# those set, dev mode prints the link to the terminal instead.
#
MAGIC_LINK_SECRET=your-random-secret-here
ADAMS_FARM_ALLOWED_EMAILS=you@example.com
